# Mermaid-first plans

Every agent **plan / architecture / multi-step proposal** must lead with **1–3 Mermaid
diagrams**, then short actionable bullets.

## Type by intent
- `flowchart` — modules, phases, ownership, import boundaries, packaging
- `sequenceDiagram` — request lifecycle, auth, discovery, cross-module contracts
- `stateDiagram` / `stateDiagram-v2` — user or entity status
- `flowchart LR` — CODEMAP current → target path renames

## Syntax
- No spaces in node IDs; use camelCase or underscores
- Quote labels that contain special characters (parentheses, commas, colons)
- Prefer subgraphs with explicit IDs: `subgraph id [Label]`

## Where diagrams live
- Product memory diagrams: `.cursor/brain/` first (see brain README)
- Team summaries: `docs/` stay thin; link to brain; mirror only high-leverage contracts
- Do not duplicate long prose across brain and docs

## Skip Mermaid when
- Pure one-file bugfix or typo with no flow / ownership / architecture impact
